    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline collapse",
          "heading": "Fiji Latui down to 12 men as Ireland XV run in nine tries",
          "body": "Fiji's second-string Latui side saw their discipline unravel against an Ireland XV in Cork on Friday night, three yellow cards in quick succession leaving them with 12 men for a spell. Isaia Lotawa went first for a no-arms tackle that conceded a penalty try, before tighthead Mesake Doge and Apisalome Kuruisaqila followed for a high tackle and a deliberate knock-on. Doge was then sent off with a second yellow for collapsing a scrum moments after returning. Ireland ran in nine tries to win 62-12, by RTÉ's count."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Rassie Erasmus handed six-match ban over match-fixing comments",
          "body": "Italy's Domingo Miotti makes debut at fly-half against Fiji. Argentina's Justo Piccardo misses France test with fatigue."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Bluenergy Stadium, Udine"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Big-game record",
          "heading": "Maro Itoje calls All Blacks clash a 'massive game for England'",
          "body": "England went into the Hillary Shield Test at Twickenham with a Nations Championship final place in play and an uncomfortable record to answer. The Guardian noted that in head coach Steve Borthwick's era they had won just four of their past 20 Tests against South Africa, New Zealand, France, Ireland and Scotland. Captain Maro Itoje called it \"a massive game for England\" and expected a furious reaction from an All Blacks side beaten by Wales the week before."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Rassie Erasmus handed six-match ban over match-fixing comments",
          "body": "Italy's Domingo Miotti makes debut at fly-half against Fiji. Argentina's Justo Piccardo misses France test with fatigue."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Backing up",
          "heading": "Rugbyrama warns Galthié's France must back up Springbok win against Argentina",
          "body": "Rugbyrama's Jérémy Fadat argues that France's historic weakness is stringing top-level performances together over several weeks. Head coach Fabien Galthié has long flagged that failing with his line \"Nous sommes des Latins.\" Fadat points to the 2026 Six Nations, which France won yet finished in a slump. The Argentina test comes eight days after the 21-19 win over South Africa, and victory would put Antoine Dupont's side into the Nations Championship final at Twickenham the following weekend."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Rassie Erasmus handed six-match ban over match-fixing comments",
          "body": "Italy's Domingo Miotti makes debut at fly-half against Fiji."
