    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ireland XV",
          "heading": "Gus McCarthy, Daniel Ryan score twice as Ireland XV rout Fiji Latui",
          "body": "Ireland's second-string XV ran in nine tries against a Fiji Latui side that imploded in Cork on Friday, picking up four yellow cards and a red in the first half and briefly playing with 12 men. Captain McCarthy and Connacht's Ryan both finished with two, while out-half Joey Carbery set up the fourth-minute opener and later dived under the posts. Paul Boyle withdrew late from the bench with a neck issue, replaced by Scott Penny, and Eoin de Buitléar was sin-binned for a hip-drop tackle."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Rassie Erasmus handed six-match ban over match-fixing comments",
          "body": "Italy's Domingo Miotti makes debut at fly-half against Fiji. Argentina's Justo Piccardo misses France test with fatigue."
