      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fly-half call",
          "heading": "Quesada handed Domingo Miotti his Italy debut at fly-half against Fiji",
          "body": "Italy head coach Gonzalo Quesada said the Montpellier No. 10's place in Saturday's test in Udine had been planned from the start, with Paolo Garbisi and Tommy Allan both told. He weighed starting Garbisi or Allan at 10 with Miotti on the bench. Injuries to wings Lynagh, Faissal, Pani and Trulla instead pushed Ange Capuozzo to the wing and Allan to full-back. The only other change from the Argentina defeat was Alessandro Ortombina starting in place of Federico Ruzza, with Quesada naming him lineout leader."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Rassie Erasmus handed six-match ban over match-fixing comments",
