          "kicker": "U20 win",
          "heading": "Scotland U20 edge Ireland 31-29 in Cork as Hamish Mather seals win",
          "body": "Scotland U20 survived five Irish tries on Friday night, as Fergus Pringle's side won on accuracy off the kicking tee. Glasgow Hawks wing Rory Caldwell scored twice. Edinburgh academy players James Dalrymple, Christian Lindsay and Rory McHaffie also crossed, and Harry Clark landed three conversions. Ireland's Paul Neary, the St Mary's out-half, sent a late conversion to level the scores wide. After the clock went red, replacement Hamish Mather ripped the ball free to secure the result."
        },
